.TH SDL_LoadSurface 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_LoadSurface \- Load a BMP, PNG or JPEG image from a file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_surface.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_Surface * SDL_LoadSurface(const char *file);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The new surface should be freed with
.BR SDL_DestroySurface ()\[char46]
Not doing so will result in a memory leak\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I file
the file to load\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to a new
.BR SDL_Surface
structure or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]4\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_DestroySurface (3),
.BR SDL_LoadSurface_IO (3)
